● The task was to fix a buggy createAsyncMemo and write vitest tests for it; the answer is written to out/cal-io/answer-opus-async-memo-rep1.txt containing only the two files.

  The fix keeps one shared promise per key in the cache (so concurrent callers dedup and fn runs once), attaches a .catch that deletes the entry and rethrows so rejections aren't cached, and leaves resolved entries in place so successes are reused.

